#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""saphira-build: build queue orchestration around buildpkg.

recipe system  = how one package is built (unchanged: recipes/<p>/recipe.sh)
autobuilder    = decides what needs building, runs it, tests it, records result

Queue is SQLite at $SAPHIRA_BUILD_STATE/queue.db (default /var/lib/saphira-build).
Per-stage verdicts: BUILD INSTALL RUNTIME POLICY OPENRC SYSTEMD IDENTITY TEST.
A package is PASS only when every applicable stage passes; PUBLISH is an
explicit human-invoked step (sign-apk-repo is the privileged boundary).

Row states: QUEUED -> BUILDING -> PASS|FAIL, plus BLOCKED (a dependency is not
satisfied) and INTERRUPTED (a build that was in flight when its builder died,
was killed, or was never restarted after a reboot). INTERRUPTED is a recorded
truth, not an absence: it carries the reason, the owning pid, the boot id, the
start time and the log directory. It is retired by `reconcile` and by daemon
startup, and re-attempted only by an explicit `retry PACKAGE` - a machine that
just lost power has not proven that every in-flight build needs repeating.
"""

